      "id": "m1",
      "title": "Implement CSV parser and row-to-object mapper",
      "status": "done",
      "plan": "Implement parseCsv and toObjects in src/csv.js. parseCsv scans character by character tracking quoted state: commas outside quotes split fields, CRLF and LF end rows outside quotes, a doubled quote inside a quoted field is one literal quote, a trailing line break adds no empty row, and empty text returns an empty array. toObjects uses row 0 as header, returns one object per later row keyed by the header, and fills missing columns with empty strings. Acceptance: quoted fields hold commas and line breaks; doubled quotes become one quote; both line endings work; no trailing empty row; empty text gives []; header-keyed objects with empty strings for short rows; the project test script passes covering all of the above.",
      "preview": null,
      "dispatch": null,
